7
00:00:55,536 --> 00:00:56,370
SCENES INVOLVING ANIMALS WERE FILMED
SAFELY WITH EXPERT ADVICE AND COOPERATION

8
00:00:56,495 --> 00:00:57,580
YEONHWARU

9
00:00:57,705 --> 00:01:01,208
[indistinct chatter]

10
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:05,379
[soft instrumental music playing
over speakers]

11
00:01:15,848 --> 00:01:17,808
[swallows, sighs]

12
00:01:17,933 --> 00:01:18,976
[door opens]

13
00:01:31,614 --> 00:01:32,781
[inhales deeply]

14
00:01:33,741 --> 00:01:34,867
[sighs]

15
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:44,335
Question.

16
00:01:46,462 --> 00:01:48,464
This is my first time here.

17
00:01:50,424 --> 00:01:51,759
What do you recommend?

18
00:01:54,345 --> 00:01:55,554
[sighs]

19
00:01:57,473 --> 00:01:58,766
Hmm, boo-boo?

20
00:02:00,726 --> 00:02:05,147
I'm not in a great mood today,
so I came in myself to have a drink.

21
00:02:05,564 --> 00:02:07,566
And now some guy's talking to me.

22
00:02:08,817 --> 00:02:10,069
Hmm?

23
00:02:10,194 --> 00:02:12,112
Just ignore him and he'll get the clue?

24
00:02:12,237 --> 00:02:14,406
-[chuckles softly]
-Okay.

25
00:02:21,455 --> 00:02:22,539
[Namgung] Hey, Sang-hun.

26
00:02:23,832 --> 00:02:26,335
Why are there
so many self-absorbed people lately?

27
00:02:26,877 --> 00:02:28,587
I just wanted to have a drink.

28
00:02:29,505 --> 00:02:32,675
It's my first time in this place,
so I asked for a recommendation.

29
00:02:33,175 --> 00:02:35,970
And now some girl is under the impression
that I'm making a move on her,

30
00:02:36,095 --> 00:02:38,430
which isn't the case. [laughs]

31
00:02:39,598 --> 00:02:41,225
Talk about a grand delusion.

32
00:02:44,019 --> 00:02:46,563
It's not fair I got rejected
before I even tried.

33
00:02:46,689 --> 00:02:47,690
But you know what?

34
00:02:52,277 --> 00:02:54,405
She's not even my type, really.

35
00:02:55,698 --> 00:02:56,991
I doubt she knows that.

36
00:02:57,700 --> 00:02:59,076
[gasps softly] Uh…

37
00:03:03,789 --> 00:03:06,250
[passionate guitar music playing]

38
00:03:06,375 --> 00:03:10,963
[both breathing heavily]

39
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:24,727
-[objects clattering]
-[panting]

40
00:03:25,477 --> 00:03:26,895
We never introduced ourselves.

41
00:03:31,066 --> 00:03:33,694
I'd go to a coffee shop
if I wanted to talk, don't you think?

42
00:03:34,403 --> 00:03:37,531
-Has anyone told you you're a bit strange?
-Hmm, I bet the same goes for you.

43
00:03:37,656 --> 00:03:38,657
Not really.

44
00:03:38,782 --> 00:03:41,201
-Usually they tell me I'm a great kisser.
-[gasps]

45
00:03:46,373 --> 00:03:50,586
[both panting, smooching]

46
00:03:54,882 --> 00:03:57,259
Who told you that?
That you're a good kisser?

47
00:03:59,344 --> 00:04:00,596
Does that really matter?

48
00:04:01,430 --> 00:04:02,639
But you're not.

49
00:04:03,265 --> 00:04:05,350
Kissing is all about
give and take, you know?

50
00:04:05,476 --> 00:04:07,811
Oh, I thought you liked it rough.

51
00:04:08,896 --> 00:04:09,980
Okay, got it.

52
00:04:10,814 --> 00:04:12,816
I can be good at the give and take.

53
00:04:14,860 --> 00:04:16,361
You know, let's stop.

54
00:04:21,617 --> 00:04:23,786
Okay, I clearly said, "Let's stop."

55
00:04:25,454 --> 00:04:26,497
[sighs]

56
00:04:30,584 --> 00:04:32,586
Do you feel bad for your boyfriend?

57
00:04:33,128 --> 00:04:34,171
Not at all.

58
00:04:35,089 --> 00:04:37,049
I just think you're not as good
as you think you are.

59
00:04:41,053 --> 00:04:42,888
-Not funny.
-Get off.

60
00:04:43,013 --> 00:04:45,474
[music fades]

61
00:04:45,599 --> 00:04:46,892
Ah, jeez.

62
00:04:49,019 --> 00:04:50,604
[inhales deeply, sighs]

63
00:04:51,522 --> 00:04:54,358
[tender piano music playing]

64
00:04:58,821 --> 00:05:00,364
You're such a mood killer.

65
00:05:02,533 --> 00:05:04,493
It's been a while. I was having fun.

66
00:05:07,287 --> 00:05:09,164
-Ah!
-[smacks lips]

67
00:05:09,289 --> 00:05:10,290
Hey!

68
00:05:14,169 --> 00:05:16,755
[Mi-do]  Namgung and I
first met when we were seven.

69
00:05:16,922 --> 00:05:19,133
[tender piano music continues]

70
00:05:20,134 --> 00:05:21,385
-[sighs]
-[spits]

71
00:05:22,636 --> 00:05:25,264
-[groans]
-[laughs]

72
00:05:25,389 --> 00:05:27,432
[both laughing]

73
00:05:28,851 --> 00:05:30,894
[Mi-do]  We've seen each other
at our absolute worst

74
00:05:31,019 --> 00:05:32,771
more times than I can count.

75
00:05:33,147 --> 00:05:34,731
[young Yeong-do]
"Do you know what solitude is?"

76
00:05:34,898 --> 00:05:37,151
-[both laugh]
-"I watched a movie called  Taxi Driver

77
00:05:37,276 --> 00:05:39,069
that taught me what it was."

78
00:05:39,194 --> 00:05:40,821
"I was nine at the time…" [gasps]

79
00:05:43,782 --> 00:05:45,701
[young Mi-do grunts]

80
00:05:46,243 --> 00:05:48,370
[Mi-do]  We went through
our turbulent teens together.

81
00:05:49,329 --> 00:05:52,082
[students shouting, laughing]

82
00:05:52,207 --> 00:05:55,377
-[groans] What is it? Why did you hit me?
-[students gasping, murmuring]

83
00:05:55,502 --> 00:05:57,462
-[young Mi-do] I'm really sorry.
-Listen, man, I'm sorry.

84
00:05:57,588 --> 00:05:58,672
[whispers] What the hell?

85
00:05:59,089 --> 00:06:00,299
-[gasps]
-[chuckles]

86
00:06:00,424 --> 00:06:02,801
[Mi-do]  We stayed friends
for a very long time.

87
00:06:03,969 --> 00:06:06,930
But then when we turned 26,
we started dating.

88
00:06:08,891 --> 00:06:11,351
And before we knew it,
ten years had gone by.

89
00:06:11,476 --> 00:06:13,020
It's not like this place is big.

90
00:06:13,854 --> 00:06:17,065
Mi-do, you're literally two steps away
from the washing machine.

91
00:06:18,483 --> 00:06:20,569
[indistinct chatter over video]

92
00:06:20,694 --> 00:06:21,945
You never clean up.

93
00:06:23,780 --> 00:06:24,823
[sighs]

94
00:06:25,782 --> 00:06:28,285
Honestly, Mi-do, you only have one mouth.

95
00:06:28,410 --> 00:06:30,871
-[cups clinking]
-Four cups, really?

96
00:06:31,663 --> 00:06:32,998
I can't live like this.

97
00:06:33,582 --> 00:06:35,876
[man over video]  Authorities
are monitoring a major storm system

98
00:06:36,001 --> 00:06:39,046
moving through several regions,
bringing heavy rain and strong winds.

99
00:06:39,171 --> 00:06:40,297
[sighs]

100
00:06:40,422 --> 00:06:43,175
Hey, I asked you to crush the cans.

101
00:06:43,675 --> 00:06:44,760
What's with this woman?

102
00:06:44,885 --> 00:06:46,762
[man]
The storm arrived earlier than expected.

103
00:06:50,015 --> 00:06:51,808
Some communities were caught off-guard.

104
00:06:51,934 --> 00:06:53,936
-Emergency crews have been called.
-[water running]

105
00:06:54,061 --> 00:06:56,063
[man]  They're working through
the evening to clear flooded roads

106
00:06:56,230 --> 00:06:57,481
and assist the residents

107
00:06:57,606 --> 00:07:00,400
in several affected areas,
according to the official report.

108
00:07:00,525 --> 00:07:03,695
-Have there been any reports of injuries?
-[music fades]

109
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:05,322
-[grunts softly]
-[man]  And what can people expect

110
00:07:05,447 --> 00:07:06,698
in the next few hours?

111
00:07:07,699 --> 00:07:10,869
Forecasters say the worst of the weather
could continue through the night.

112
00:07:10,994 --> 00:07:12,246
Residents of low-lying areas

113
00:07:12,371 --> 00:07:14,206
-are being urged to stayed indoors.
-[sighs]

114
00:07:14,706 --> 00:07:17,834
Director Lee, why are you
in such a bad mood lately?

115
00:07:18,585 --> 00:07:21,838
[man]  Officials are also warning drivers
not to attempt to cross flooded roads.

116
00:07:22,005 --> 00:07:24,508
One, production was delayed by two months.

117
00:07:24,633 --> 00:07:27,010
Two, you went to the edit room,
watched the footage,

118
00:07:27,135 --> 00:07:29,179
and Song Hae-na's acting's terrible.

119
00:07:29,304 --> 00:07:32,224
Three, the producers keep
rejecting your music director.

120
00:07:32,391 --> 00:07:33,892
[man continues speaking indistinctly
over video]

121
00:07:34,059 --> 00:07:36,311
Four, I haven't kissed you.

122
00:07:36,436 --> 00:07:37,938
[scoffs]

123
00:07:38,063 --> 00:07:40,357
[chuckles] I knew it was four.

124
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:43,235
Or five.

125
00:07:43,360 --> 00:07:45,904
I missed out on our shrimp toast
because you got home late.

126
00:07:47,948 --> 00:07:50,033
[man]  Are schools expected
to remain open tomorrow?

127
00:07:50,158 --> 00:07:52,119
Any communication about this
from the authorities?

128
00:07:52,786 --> 00:07:53,912
[inhales sharply]

129
00:07:54,663 --> 00:07:55,956
I can order chicken.

130
00:07:56,081 --> 00:07:57,791
[man]  All right.
We'll continue to follow this story…

131
00:07:57,916 --> 00:07:58,834
[gulps]

132
00:07:59,042 --> 00:08:03,130
My treat? All combo.
Mustard, yogurt, garlic sauce.

133
00:08:04,089 --> 00:08:05,882
-And double cheese sticks?
-Okay, deal.

134
00:08:06,008 --> 00:08:09,177
Hmm. [chuckles]

135
00:08:10,804 --> 00:08:13,265
You were against using CGI snow anyway.

136
00:08:14,182 --> 00:08:17,686
Although it sucks that the producers
decided without telling you.

137
00:08:18,812 --> 00:08:20,731
But it turned out fine, right?

138
00:08:20,856 --> 00:08:23,567
Director Lee Mi-do
is known for mise-en-scène.

139
00:08:23,734 --> 00:08:25,777
Just do your thing and kill it.

140
00:08:25,902 --> 00:08:28,488
[man continues speaking indistinctly
over video]

141
00:08:31,033 --> 00:08:32,326
Do you think I should just end it?

142
00:08:34,161 --> 00:08:36,288
Mm. Go ahead.

143
00:08:39,291 --> 00:08:40,334
[clicks tongue]

144
00:08:40,709 --> 00:08:45,505
-[gentle guitar music playing]
-[vocalist singing in Korean]

145
00:08:45,630 --> 00:08:51,511
1. WILL TEN YEARS TOGETHER
END IN MARRIAGE OR A BREAKUP?

146
00:08:53,972 --> 00:08:56,183
NAMGUNG-TUSH

147
00:08:56,308 --> 00:08:59,644
[cell phone vibrating]

148
00:09:02,981 --> 00:09:04,358
[groans]

149
00:09:05,067 --> 00:09:07,486
[groans] Wakey, wakey.

150
00:09:08,653 --> 00:09:11,948
[groans] I love you, sweetie. Ciao, ciao.

151
00:09:14,201 --> 00:09:16,244
I love you, sweetie. Ciao.

152
00:09:20,999 --> 00:09:21,958
Huh.

153
00:09:32,469 --> 00:09:34,429
[yawns]

154
00:09:35,305 --> 00:09:37,140
[keypad beeping]

155
00:09:41,478 --> 00:09:42,646
[coughs]

156
00:09:42,771 --> 00:09:45,357
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

157
00:10:02,582 --> 00:10:05,043
-Hey! [sighs]
-[shower running]

158
00:10:05,168 --> 00:10:07,504
SWEET DELIGHT FROM GOOD INGREDIENTS

159
00:10:07,629 --> 00:10:08,713
[Hae-na over video]  Guess what?

160
00:10:08,839 --> 00:10:10,924
Today I'm gonna show you
the set of the movie  No Heart.

161
00:10:11,091 --> 00:10:13,260
-[breathes deeply]
-[Yeong-rae]  Hae-na?

162
00:10:13,385 --> 00:10:15,095
[Hae-na]  Look, the director!

163
00:10:16,179 --> 00:10:18,390
Huh? Didn't you tell her
no personal filming?

164
00:10:18,515 --> 00:10:19,975
I told the manager since the beginning,

165
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:21,935
but I'm sorry, I'll go ahead
and tell them again.

166
00:10:22,686 --> 00:10:24,438
-[sighs]
-[Mi-do]  Because of the genre,

167
00:10:24,563 --> 00:10:25,730
even a prop can be a spoiler,

168
00:10:25,856 --> 00:10:28,316
so personal filming
by staff and crew isn't allowed.

169
00:10:28,442 --> 00:10:31,319
Get the video you just took cleared
by production first.

170
00:10:34,156 --> 00:10:36,116
[Hae-na]  The director seems a little mad.

171
00:10:36,241 --> 00:10:39,619
Now I need to make sure it gets cleared
so I can upload it for you.

172
00:10:39,744 --> 00:10:40,745
CLEARED!

173
00:10:40,871 --> 00:10:43,373
I'M SO HAPPY TO SHOW YOU
A GLIMPSE OF THE SET!

174
00:10:44,166 --> 00:10:47,377
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

175
00:10:47,502 --> 00:10:49,087
DIRECTORS CAN'T BE SO AUTHORITARIAN

176
00:10:49,212 --> 00:10:50,547
SHE DIDN'T HAVE TO DO THAT

177
00:10:50,672 --> 00:10:51,882
DID YOU SEE HER EYES?

178
00:10:52,007 --> 00:10:54,426
[commenter 1]  She directed the indie film
After Spring Comes Summer,

179
00:10:54,551 --> 00:10:57,012
-the one starring Gong Ji-Seok.
-[music concludes]

180
00:10:57,137 --> 00:10:59,014
[Namgung]  After Spring Comes Winter.

181
00:10:59,514 --> 00:11:01,933
[commenter 2]  Didn't she win an award
before Bong Joon-ho?

182
00:11:02,058 --> 00:11:04,352
[Namgung]  In 2018,
she won at Florence Shorts,

183
00:11:04,478 --> 00:11:06,730
the first Asian woman
to ever achieve that.

184
00:11:06,855 --> 00:11:08,273
[commenter 3]
The director looks really young,

185
00:11:08,398 --> 00:11:10,192
even younger than Song Hae-na.

186
00:11:11,067 --> 00:11:15,739
-Uh, no, I don't think so.
-[hums] Ah, jeez.

187
00:11:15,864 --> 00:11:20,368
[gasps] Please, wait, boss, wait.
Listen to me, please. Sir.

188
00:11:20,494 --> 00:11:22,913
-[hesitates]
-Uh…

189
00:11:23,038 --> 00:11:25,332
I almost broke my back hauling those bags.
Take responsibility.

190
00:11:25,457 --> 00:11:29,085
[laughs] Take responsibility?
What does that have to do with me?

191
00:11:29,211 --> 00:11:32,297
Uh, wait, sir. I was wiping down
the conveyor belt, and look.

192
00:11:32,797 --> 00:11:33,798
And I got hurt.

193
00:11:33,924 --> 00:11:35,967
I was washing trays,
and now my joints hurt.

194
00:11:36,134 --> 00:11:37,135
It looks all right.

195
00:11:38,094 --> 00:11:40,096
Really? What do you mean, sir?

196
00:11:40,222 --> 00:11:42,432
Thirty minutes ago, I started feeling pain
in my carpal tunnel.

197
00:11:42,557 --> 00:11:44,392
God, the pain was unbearable. [chuckles]

198
00:11:44,518 --> 00:11:46,186
I know you're doing this
because your team

199
00:11:46,311 --> 00:11:48,813
got the fourth
Hatguma Chips sample, right?

200
00:11:50,273 --> 00:11:53,109
There's no difference at all.
I told you that.

201
00:11:53,235 --> 00:11:54,486
Yes, there is. I notice.

202
00:11:54,611 --> 00:11:57,322
[indistinct chatter]

203
00:11:57,447 --> 00:12:00,992
Our batch was the only one
preceded by Hoho Bakchip.

204
00:12:01,117 --> 00:12:02,327
They're milk-fat based,

205
00:12:02,452 --> 00:12:05,580
so no matter how much I CIP,
there's cross-contamination.

206
00:12:05,705 --> 00:12:06,706
[factory manager] So what?

207
00:12:06,915 --> 00:12:10,335
The fifth batch of Hoho Bakchip
is also scheduled before.

208
00:12:11,753 --> 00:12:15,966
[sighs] You want me to change it?
It's hard to change schedules at year-end.

209
00:12:16,091 --> 00:12:19,094
You know what I think? You think I'm weak.

210
00:12:19,219 --> 00:12:21,263
That's why you're acting
so confident, right?

211
00:12:21,388 --> 00:12:24,641
Not at all. I'm just saving up your debt.

212
00:12:26,268 --> 00:12:28,562
-[inhales deeply, sighs]
-[bright quirky music playing]

213
00:12:28,687 --> 00:12:30,647
I can buy you a Celint 18-year-old scotch

214
00:12:30,772 --> 00:12:33,149
-like Assistant Manager Shin.
-[scoffs]

215
00:12:33,275 --> 00:12:35,527
[Namgung] But I wonder
if I really have to go that far.

216
00:12:35,652 --> 00:12:37,779
-And honestly, I don't want to.
-[scoffs]

217
00:12:37,904 --> 00:12:40,240
-Listen, I hate being pathetic.
-[sighs]

218
00:12:40,699 --> 00:12:43,368
Although, I'm confident in using my body.

219
00:12:43,493 --> 00:12:44,661
What are you talking about?

220
00:12:45,453 --> 00:12:47,122
Tell me, why'd you do all that?

221
00:12:47,247 --> 00:12:48,582
-Who asked you to volunteer?
-Oh, no.

222
00:12:48,707 --> 00:12:49,666
[gasps]

223
00:12:50,250 --> 00:12:51,501
Where did it go?

224
00:12:51,626 --> 00:12:54,337
Huh? I'm sure it was here, or not.

225
00:12:54,462 --> 00:12:55,672
-What?
-I guess I left it at home.

226
00:12:55,797 --> 00:12:57,591
-Missing something? What?
-Have you seen it?

227
00:12:57,716 --> 00:12:59,301
Your conscience, manager.

228
00:12:59,426 --> 00:13:01,261
Jeez, you're such a…

229
00:13:02,345 --> 00:13:03,930
If you work me to the bone for a week,

230
00:13:04,055 --> 00:13:06,725
you should be able
to calculate the price properly.

231
00:13:07,517 --> 00:13:08,893
-Anyway, using my hourly wage…
-[scoffs]

232
00:13:09,019 --> 00:13:10,228
…calculated for my base salary,

233
00:13:10,353 --> 00:13:13,315
three hours a day, four on Thursday,
and I came after work.

234
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:17,068
-[scoffs]
-If you multiply that by seven… [gasps]

235
00:13:17,902 --> 00:13:21,531
I was even more expensive
than a Celint 18-year-old scotch.

236
00:13:21,656 --> 00:13:23,325
That's 370,000 won.

237
00:13:23,992 --> 00:13:26,911
-[factory manager sighs]
-[gasps] My God, that's a lot, huh?

238
00:13:27,996 --> 00:13:29,039
[factory manager sighs]

239
00:13:29,164 --> 00:13:31,041
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

240
00:13:31,166 --> 00:13:33,209
[bright quirky music continues]

241
00:13:33,335 --> 00:13:34,628
[sighs]

242
00:13:38,923 --> 00:13:41,426
[intriguing musical sting]

243
00:13:41,551 --> 00:13:43,720
[groans, sighs]

244
00:13:47,557 --> 00:13:48,600
[smooching sound effect]

245
00:13:51,519 --> 00:13:53,229
How long is this gonna go on?

246
00:13:53,355 --> 00:13:55,315
-Until you finally give in.
-[inhales deeply]

247
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,525
The executives already fixed it.
How can we change it?

248
00:13:57,651 --> 00:14:00,362
-Will you take responsibility if it fails?
-That's your job, isn't it?

249
00:14:00,487 --> 00:14:02,864
You get paid two million more than me.

250
00:14:02,989 --> 00:14:05,533
Seriously? Why?

251
00:14:06,242 --> 00:14:08,328
-Ah, shut it.
-[sighs]

252
00:14:08,453 --> 00:14:10,664
-[sighs] Okay, fine.
-[music fades]

253
00:14:10,789 --> 00:14:13,208
I admit there's a slight difference
in sweetness,

254
00:14:13,333 --> 00:14:16,294
but the internal survey shows
similar responses overall,

255
00:14:16,419 --> 00:14:17,587
from the first to fourth batch.

256
00:14:17,712 --> 00:14:19,881
So statistically,
there's no real difference.

257
00:14:21,758 --> 00:14:24,260
These are the internal survey comments
for Hatguma Chips.

258
00:14:24,386 --> 00:14:26,012
Take a look. Here.

259
00:14:27,472 --> 00:14:28,515
[groans]

260
00:14:29,182 --> 00:14:30,433
HATGUMA CHIPS
INTERNAL SURVEY RESULTS

261
00:14:33,103 --> 00:14:36,564
[Su-a]  There isn't sweet potato flavor.
Aftertaste is the worst.

262
00:14:36,690 --> 00:14:38,358
At this rate,
it'll flop without even launching.

263
00:14:38,483 --> 00:14:40,193
-What's this?
-[Su-a]  My condolences.

264
00:14:40,318 --> 00:14:42,070
Did you write this?
It's exactly what you just said.

265
00:14:42,195 --> 00:14:44,406
I know, right? I even thought,

266
00:14:44,531 --> 00:14:46,449
"Huh? Did I sabotage this while drunk?"

267
00:14:46,574 --> 00:14:49,327
[whimsical instrumental music playing]

268
00:14:49,452 --> 00:14:52,080
I think you forgot this
because you're aging, sir.

269
00:14:52,205 --> 00:14:54,290
Something similar happened
with Hot Choco Chips.

270
00:14:54,416 --> 00:14:56,876
Guess who noticed
the steam input error back then?

271
00:14:57,460 --> 00:15:01,423
I hate to say this myself,
but I caught it.

272
00:15:01,881 --> 00:15:03,133
[Sang-hun] Holy moly.

273
00:15:03,258 --> 00:15:06,386
So that's the Hot Choco Chips
origin story?

274
00:15:06,511 --> 00:15:08,430
It's an honor to hear it.
I can't believe it.

275
00:15:08,596 --> 00:15:09,889
-Stop it.
-[whip cracking sound effect]

276
00:15:15,228 --> 00:15:19,190
[sighs] I worked all week
to change the factory schedule.

277
00:15:19,357 --> 00:15:21,526
[scoffs] Jeez, all for nothing.

278
00:15:22,944 --> 00:15:26,072
Okay. November, first week.
No more delays.

279
00:15:26,197 --> 00:15:28,908
-[groans] Hey, get off! [grunts]
-[cell phone vibrating]

280
00:15:29,033 --> 00:15:30,160
Just a minute.

281
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:31,536
YEONHUI-DONG TWIN FISTS

282
00:15:31,661 --> 00:15:33,663
-[Ho-sik] Get back to work. Right now.
-I'll be right back.

283
00:15:33,788 --> 00:15:36,082
-Oh, what a pain.
-[music concludes]

284
00:15:36,207 --> 00:15:38,293
QUEENS HAIR SALON

285
00:15:38,418 --> 00:15:40,587
-[Namgung] Oh, looks delicious.
-[Mi-do] Oh, it's so good.

286
00:15:40,712 --> 00:15:42,297
[cutlery clinking]

287
00:15:44,048 --> 00:15:45,008
[Namgung slurps]

288
00:15:46,551 --> 00:15:47,677
[Mi-do] So good.

289
00:15:47,844 --> 00:15:50,722
-[Namgung chews, sighs] Oh, spinach.
-[Mi-do] Mm.

290
00:15:50,847 --> 00:15:51,890
Eat your spinach.

291
00:15:52,056 --> 00:15:54,267
[both munching]

292
00:15:54,392 --> 00:15:55,435
You two.

293
00:15:56,186 --> 00:15:57,979
-[Mi-do sighs]
-Decide right now.

294
00:15:58,897 --> 00:16:03,318
Are you tying the knot or calling it off?
You gotta choose.

295
00:16:05,278 --> 00:16:08,239
[Yeong-do scoffs] Uh, Mom, are you crazy?

296
00:16:08,364 --> 00:16:10,825
He has a great salary,
full-time corporate job,

297
00:16:10,950 --> 00:16:11,868
and solid gains.

298
00:16:11,993 --> 00:16:15,663
Why would Namgung settle for someone
who doesn't even get insurance?

299
00:16:16,456 --> 00:16:19,250
-Does that make sense?
-Mom, listen.

300
00:16:19,375 --> 00:16:21,419
Namgung's happiness
is just as important as--

301
00:16:21,544 --> 00:16:23,213
-[grunts]
-[both groan]

302
00:16:23,338 --> 00:16:24,756
It's true, Mom!

303
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:28,593
[Yeong-do sighs]

304
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:32,055
[sighs]

305
00:16:33,306 --> 00:16:37,894
Listen… quit playing dumb,
you two. [sighs]

306
00:16:38,019 --> 00:16:40,355
[quirky piano music playing]

307
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:43,107
Um, Gang Dong-won is almost in.
We have Chinese investors, too.

308
00:16:43,233 --> 00:16:44,234
29-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

309
00:16:44,359 --> 00:16:46,110
It's happening faster than I thought.

310
00:16:46,236 --> 00:16:48,696
Anyway, you just keep looking
for an apartment.

311
00:16:48,863 --> 00:16:50,240
[munches]

312
00:16:50,365 --> 00:16:52,700
[gasps] Gong Yoo is gonna do it!

313
00:16:52,826 --> 00:16:54,077
"Drama or movie?" That was the question.

314
00:16:54,202 --> 00:16:55,203
30-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

315
00:16:55,370 --> 00:16:57,247
He'll make a decision soon,
and we'll sign next week.

316
00:16:57,372 --> 00:16:58,832
He's in.

317
00:16:58,957 --> 00:17:00,875
Keep looking for that apartment, honey.

318
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:04,128
[gasps] He didn't sign!
Do you think I wanted this?

319
00:17:04,254 --> 00:17:05,672
The production company suddenly folded.

320
00:17:05,797 --> 00:17:06,631
32-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

321
00:17:06,756 --> 00:17:09,425
Whatever.
We're shaking off the bad luck. [gasps]

322
00:17:10,343 --> 00:17:14,222
I'm serious, okay? Listen closely.
That apartment is going to be ours.

323
00:17:14,347 --> 00:17:15,431
[breathes heavily]

324
00:17:16,057 --> 00:17:17,559
33-YEAR-OLD LEE MI-DO

325
00:17:17,684 --> 00:17:20,311
So, the investors' response
isn't bad, you know?

326
00:17:21,104 --> 00:17:22,730
I'm sure that they are…

327
00:17:24,232 --> 00:17:25,567
I know it's not closed yet,

328
00:17:25,692 --> 00:17:29,320
but we'll keep looking
for that apart-- Ah!

329
00:17:32,031 --> 00:17:34,826
-[music fades]
-Oh, come on. There's no rush.

330
00:17:34,993 --> 00:17:36,244
[sword drawing sound effect]

331
00:17:37,412 --> 00:17:38,288
[hesitates]

332
00:17:38,413 --> 00:17:40,248
-Good point. You better listen.
-[whimsical guitar music playing]

333
00:17:40,373 --> 00:17:41,374
Your mom says that out of love,

334
00:17:41,499 --> 00:17:42,750
-we should…
-[sword drawing sound effect]

335
00:17:43,793 --> 00:17:46,170
-Hey, I'm with you. Just ignore it.
-[sighs]

336
00:17:48,131 --> 00:17:49,757
[chuckles softly] Here.

337
00:17:50,925 --> 00:17:54,304
Ma'am, you saw all the articles
about Mi-do's movie, right?

338
00:17:54,429 --> 00:17:58,224
This time it's for real.
I know it. [grunts]

339
00:18:00,226 --> 00:18:02,687
Oh, Mom, I saw some articles, too.

340
00:18:02,812 --> 00:18:04,606
Song Hae-na posted it online.

341
00:18:04,731 --> 00:18:05,690
-Oh.
-[Wan-do] Yeah.

342
00:18:05,815 --> 00:18:08,151
Although filming a movie
doesn't mean it'll get finished.

343
00:18:09,068 --> 00:18:12,196
Ma, so many movies
these days never actually come out.

344
00:18:12,322 --> 00:18:13,531
And that's a shame bec…

345
00:18:15,950 --> 00:18:17,035
[gulps]

346
00:18:17,660 --> 00:18:19,913
Anyway, I'm sure it's real this time.

347
00:18:20,496 --> 00:18:22,206
Don't stress out Lee Mi-do.

348
00:18:22,332 --> 00:18:25,126
You may look down on her,
but out there, she's respected.

349
00:18:25,251 --> 00:18:26,294
Enough.

350
00:18:27,420 --> 00:18:29,005
You two promised, right?

351
00:18:29,130 --> 00:18:32,175
That you'd get married
once she becomes a director?

352
00:18:32,300 --> 00:18:33,635
This is not a joke.

353
00:18:34,177 --> 00:18:35,553
Six months.

354
00:18:36,012 --> 00:18:37,513
-[sighs]
-Uh…

355
00:18:39,807 --> 00:18:43,978
There's a little issue,
'cause Mi-do's filming got delayed

356
00:18:44,103 --> 00:18:47,106
because of the snowy mountain
and the process of editing--

357
00:18:47,231 --> 00:18:48,524
-[music concludes]
-If you keep overthinking it,

358
00:18:48,650 --> 00:18:49,609
you'll never do it.

359
00:18:49,734 --> 00:18:51,444
Either it works or you make it work.

360
00:18:51,569 --> 00:18:54,405
But stop making excuses.
Get married or break up.

361
00:18:54,530 --> 00:18:56,366
-[slams spoon]
-[sighs]

362
00:18:56,991 --> 00:19:00,161
Look at you. I just said what I thought,
but you can't handle it.

363
00:19:00,286 --> 00:19:01,621
That temper of yours.

364
00:19:01,746 --> 00:19:02,747
Antacid?

365
00:19:03,456 --> 00:19:05,583
Does your tummy hurt? You okay?

366
00:19:09,170 --> 00:19:10,630
Hey, are you…

367
00:19:11,339 --> 00:19:12,382
Not at all.

368
00:19:12,507 --> 00:19:14,592
You shouldn't take any medicine.
You never know.

369
00:19:14,717 --> 00:19:16,094
Didn't you hear, Mom? I said no.

370
00:19:16,219 --> 00:19:19,806
How can you be so sure, huh?
It never hurts to be careful.

371
00:19:19,931 --> 00:19:21,182
We haven't had sex in six months.

372
00:19:21,307 --> 00:19:23,518
[splutters, coughs]

373
00:19:23,643 --> 00:19:26,562
[whimsical guitar music playing]

374
00:19:27,397 --> 00:19:29,023
[clears throat]

375
00:19:29,148 --> 00:19:31,859
Hey, why would you say
that in front of your mom?

376
00:19:31,985 --> 00:19:34,779
-Are you out of your mind or what?
-[music concludes]

377
00:19:34,904 --> 00:19:39,575
If I hadn't, we'd be arguing over Guam
or Cebu for our honeymoon by now.

378
00:19:39,701 --> 00:19:41,369
You're welcome, okay?

379
00:19:41,494 --> 00:19:42,745
You don't say?

380
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:45,540
God, you oversharing
is just what I needed.

381
00:19:47,250 --> 00:19:50,044
-Well, I wasn't lying, was I?
-Hey, that's not…

382
00:19:52,005 --> 00:19:53,965
We've both been busy lately, so…

383
00:19:56,342 --> 00:19:57,427
[inhales sharply]

384
00:19:58,428 --> 00:19:59,846
That long already?

385
00:20:01,014 --> 00:20:03,725
-Two, and then--
-[gasps] Stop counting, okay?

386
00:20:03,891 --> 00:20:05,560
[sighs] Well, if you say so.

387
00:20:06,477 --> 00:20:07,395
[sighs]

388
00:20:07,520 --> 00:20:11,774
I told you not to go, didn't I?
My mom's never gonna let this go.

389
00:20:13,026 --> 00:20:16,070
I really think that she's just doing that
because she's worried about you.

390
00:20:20,950 --> 00:20:23,119
It's just delayed because of your film.

391
00:20:24,495 --> 00:20:26,289
We've talked about the wedding.

392
00:20:29,208 --> 00:20:31,711
What do you mean?
You actually want to tie the knot?

393
00:20:31,836 --> 00:20:34,172
Mm. Of course I do.

394
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:38,926
You don't?

395
00:20:39,052 --> 00:20:43,306
[car horn blares, fades]

396
00:20:47,143 --> 00:20:49,771
It's not that I don't want to.
I'm just scared.

397
00:20:50,772 --> 00:20:52,356
[sighs] Getting married…

398
00:20:52,482 --> 00:20:54,275
[sighs]
…it's ending the second act of life

399
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,985
and entering the third act,

400
00:20:56,110 --> 00:20:58,237
but I feel like my second act
isn't even done yet.

401
00:20:59,655 --> 00:21:02,200
I mean, sure,
I'm shooting a movie right now.

402
00:21:02,867 --> 00:21:04,118
I don't know how it'll turn out.

403
00:21:08,081 --> 00:21:09,165
[sighs]

404
00:21:13,086 --> 00:21:14,462
I know what I'm like.

405
00:21:16,297 --> 00:21:18,591
I'm selfish and I only care about myself.

406
00:21:19,509 --> 00:21:21,135
And I know if I marry you,

407
00:21:21,302 --> 00:21:24,138
the comfort you give me
would be enough for me to settle.

408
00:21:25,556 --> 00:21:27,934
I'll stop writing
and live off you like a leech.

409
00:21:28,059 --> 00:21:31,229
But I can't do that.
A nightmare, that's what that sounds like.

410
00:21:32,897 --> 00:21:35,525
So I was just a leech to you then, huh?

411
00:21:35,650 --> 00:21:36,651
Hey!

412
00:21:37,193 --> 00:21:38,194
That's the thing.

413
00:21:39,445 --> 00:21:40,738
That's not being a leech.

414
00:21:41,572 --> 00:21:43,991
Call it reliance, coexistence, or care.

415
00:21:44,117 --> 00:21:45,284
I didn't mean…

416
00:21:46,661 --> 00:21:48,454
Drink this. Your tummy hurts.

417
00:21:54,001 --> 00:21:55,962
I have leftover abalone. Do you want it?

418
00:21:56,671 --> 00:21:58,464
You were just picking
at your food earlier.

419
00:22:06,681 --> 00:22:08,724
I don't want that. Make fried rice.

420
00:22:08,850 --> 00:22:11,477
Your tummy hurts. Just eat this.

421
00:22:16,816 --> 00:22:18,067
Do you remember that day?

422
00:22:19,777 --> 00:22:22,029
In ninth grade during summer break?

423
00:22:25,324 --> 00:22:26,450
[gentle piano music playing]

424
00:22:26,576 --> 00:22:30,413
[pants]

425
00:22:32,665 --> 00:22:33,791
EMERGENCY ROOM

426
00:22:33,958 --> 00:22:35,334
This way. This way.

427
00:22:36,377 --> 00:22:38,296
[Namgung]  I was running
with you on my back.

428
00:22:39,172 --> 00:22:41,591
And you didn't feel heavy at all.

429
00:22:41,716 --> 00:22:43,092
[doctor] Lee Mi-do! Lee Mi-do!

430
00:22:47,430 --> 00:22:49,265
-Run a blood test.
-[nurse] Yes, doctor.

431
00:22:50,099 --> 00:22:51,267
I'll take your temperature.

432
00:22:52,894 --> 00:22:54,145
[Namgung]  And I found out later…

433
00:22:56,230 --> 00:23:00,276
I carried you six miles
in just 30 minutes.

434
00:23:03,321 --> 00:23:05,364
So don't say anything about being a leech.

435
00:23:06,574 --> 00:23:08,409
When you're clinging to my back…

436
00:23:10,620 --> 00:23:11,913
that's when I'm strongest.

437
00:23:15,208 --> 00:23:17,043
You're like… [inhales sharply]

438
00:23:17,210 --> 00:23:19,378
…a booster.
You keep me moving forward.

439
00:23:25,676 --> 00:23:27,553
My movie might flop this time.

440
00:23:27,678 --> 00:23:29,639
-Is that okay?
-Yeah.

441
00:23:29,805 --> 00:23:32,099
Even if breathing
while holding your back, is that…

442
00:23:32,225 --> 00:23:34,810
-Mm-hmm. That's fine.
-And if I kill someone?

443
00:23:35,436 --> 00:23:36,270
Hey.

444
00:23:37,104 --> 00:23:40,399
-I said I'd do anything for you, but…
-Answer me.

445
00:23:45,696 --> 00:23:46,572
Well…

446
00:23:48,241 --> 00:23:49,617
first I'd curse you out.

447
00:23:51,327 --> 00:23:52,453
Really bad.

448
00:24:00,378 --> 00:24:02,505
Then I'd bring you stuff in jail.
[chuckles softly]

449
00:24:04,507 --> 00:24:08,344
[knife chopping]

450
00:24:09,262 --> 00:24:10,638
[gasps] The carrots.

451
00:24:11,389 --> 00:24:13,432
I hate the crunch.
Chop them smaller, okay?

452
00:24:13,557 --> 00:24:14,809
Yeah, yeah.

453
00:24:31,325 --> 00:24:32,868
[Namgung] Why are you awake?

454
00:24:35,454 --> 00:24:36,664
Namgung.

455
00:24:38,708 --> 00:24:41,419
Is it really okay if my movie fails?

456
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,380
[inhales deeply]

457
00:24:49,844 --> 00:24:50,970
Of course.

458
00:24:52,596 --> 00:24:54,098
It's totally fine.

459
00:24:55,057 --> 00:24:57,727
Just do your best with no regrets.

460
00:25:00,021 --> 00:25:01,188
Just do that.

461
00:25:02,023 --> 00:25:04,400
[music concludes]

462
00:25:09,947 --> 00:25:11,574
[shower running]

463
00:25:19,623 --> 00:25:21,751
[actor moaning]

464
00:25:22,877 --> 00:25:27,757
[moaning continues in higher pitch]

465
00:25:29,383 --> 00:25:31,719
-[walkie-talkie beeps]
-Cut. Let's take a short break.

466
00:25:31,844 --> 00:25:34,847
-[crew member 1] We're taking a break.
-[crew members sighing]

467
00:25:34,972 --> 00:25:37,475
[indistinct chatter]

468
00:25:38,434 --> 00:25:40,227
24 HOURS IS NEVER ENOUGH

469
00:25:40,353 --> 00:25:42,146
[inhales deeply, sighs]

470
00:25:42,271 --> 00:25:45,149
Uh, I'm really sorry.
This kind of movie is a first for me.

471
00:25:45,274 --> 00:25:47,068
[breathes shakily]

472
00:25:47,234 --> 00:25:50,821
Maybe you don't know this, but I debuted
in Director Hwang Sun-gi's  Manifesto.

473
00:25:50,946 --> 00:25:52,656
I was a rising star in Chungmuro.

474
00:25:52,782 --> 00:25:55,868
I appeared in a lot of dramas.
I'm talking too much.

475
00:25:56,786 --> 00:25:59,789
-[sighs]
-My guess is D flat or E?

476
00:26:01,415 --> 00:26:03,626
-What?
-Ah, ah…

477
00:26:03,793 --> 00:26:04,794
[in higher pitch] …ah.

478
00:26:04,919 --> 00:26:07,338
Uh-huh. It's the pitch. Can you do that?

479
00:26:08,130 --> 00:26:11,175
-[lowering pitch] Ah, ah, ah.
-Huh.

480
00:26:11,300 --> 00:26:13,928
If the man's moans are higher pitched
than the woman's,

481
00:26:14,053 --> 00:26:18,224
-it doesn't work, right?
-Ah, ah. Huh.

482
00:26:18,349 --> 00:26:20,935
Okay, in five minutes,
we'll resume shooting.

483
00:26:21,060 --> 00:26:21,936
[crew member 2] Copy that.

484
00:26:22,103 --> 00:26:23,938
[dramatic classical music playing
over speakers]

485
00:26:24,063 --> 00:26:27,108
[Yeon-ju] The CEO also feels bad
about this whole situation.

486
00:26:27,233 --> 00:26:30,653
Articles of your departure
will go out once we settle.

487
00:26:30,778 --> 00:26:32,780
Oh, as for your replacement,

488
00:26:32,947 --> 00:26:36,659
we're trying to find someone whose style
matches your creative approach.

489
00:26:37,201 --> 00:26:39,453
Because of the on-location
snow scene shoot,

490
00:26:39,578 --> 00:26:42,873
we have to wait a month anyway,
so there's no rush.

491
00:26:43,666 --> 00:26:46,544
Tell me, do you have questions?

492
00:26:47,586 --> 00:26:51,424
I've watched for 30 minutes,
and there are four low angle shots.

493
00:26:54,969 --> 00:26:57,972
-About time.
-[actor]  Hey, why are you here?

494
00:26:58,722 --> 00:27:00,391
[Yeon-ju] That's because Song Hae-na
needed time

495
00:27:00,516 --> 00:27:02,643
to get her nose surgery corrected.

496
00:27:02,768 --> 00:27:05,104
-[scoffs]
-[actor]  What do you mean?

497
00:27:05,229 --> 00:27:06,564
-[music fades]
-Anyway, honestly,

498
00:27:06,689 --> 00:27:09,525
I didn't realize you were such
a hard worker until now.

499
00:27:09,650 --> 00:27:11,986
It hasn't even been two weeks
since you left the film,

500
00:27:12,528 --> 00:27:14,488
and you're already on your next project.

501
00:27:15,156 --> 00:27:16,699
It's extraordinary.

502
00:27:16,824 --> 00:27:17,867
Well… [sighs]

503
00:27:17,992 --> 00:27:21,787
…I've got a messy court battle
coming up soon, and I can't afford it.

504
00:27:22,788 --> 00:27:23,873
Mm-hmm.

505
00:27:25,207 --> 00:27:27,376
[Hae-na over TV]
I don't know why I can't forget you.

506
00:27:28,127 --> 00:27:29,170
Is there something else?

507
00:27:30,880 --> 00:27:33,340
We all want to thank you
for everything you've done, ma'am.

508
00:27:38,554 --> 00:27:40,306
Now I won't talk as a producer.

509
00:27:40,431 --> 00:27:42,475
Listen to me
as a high school friend, okay?

510
00:27:44,977 --> 00:27:47,438
-We're friends?
-As a classmate, then.

511
00:27:48,147 --> 00:27:50,816
I'm trying to be kind,
so please listen closely.

512
00:27:50,941 --> 00:27:52,234
Try that for just a second.

513
00:27:53,527 --> 00:27:54,612
[sighs]

514
00:27:55,321 --> 00:27:58,157
A lawyer will call you this week
about the settlement.

515
00:27:58,282 --> 00:28:01,118
-Don't try to go to court. Just sign it.
-No.

516
00:28:01,660 --> 00:28:04,872
It'll be a messy fight
if you decide to take it to court.

517
00:28:04,997 --> 00:28:06,832
Do you want to turn this into a bloodbath?

518
00:28:06,957 --> 00:28:08,501
That's why I do it, you know?

519
00:28:10,002 --> 00:28:12,546
-[pensive music playing]
-Everything is a mess now.

520
00:28:12,671 --> 00:28:15,633
I'm as low as it gets,
and that won't change a thing.

521
00:28:15,758 --> 00:28:16,967
[Yeon-ju sighs]

522
00:28:19,345 --> 00:28:20,596
[sighs]

523
00:28:20,721 --> 00:28:23,349
Thanks for the advice. Not that it helped.

524
00:28:27,353 --> 00:28:28,187
[sighs]

525
00:28:43,077 --> 00:28:45,538
[water burbling]

526
00:28:49,375 --> 00:28:52,461
TWO WEEKS AGO

527
00:28:52,670 --> 00:28:54,046
[music fades]

528
00:28:58,259 --> 00:29:00,344
Hey, like we prepped,
we need some tracking shots.

529
00:29:00,469 --> 00:29:02,513
Director, I have a message

530
00:29:02,638 --> 00:29:04,306
from Song Hae-na
saying she can't film today.

531
00:29:05,516 --> 00:29:06,517
And why?

532
00:29:07,184 --> 00:29:09,353
-Because of a private brand event today.
-[sighs]

533
00:29:09,478 --> 00:29:10,938
[Yeong-rae] Her manager forgot about it.

534
00:29:11,855 --> 00:29:13,357
[sighs] I can't.

535
00:29:13,482 --> 00:29:16,402
[upbeat instrumental music playing]

536
00:29:16,527 --> 00:29:19,113
[grunts] What? What? What is it?

537
00:29:22,533 --> 00:29:23,867
[manager] Director, wait right there.

538
00:29:24,451 --> 00:29:25,869
Hold on, please.

539
00:29:27,454 --> 00:29:29,748
Allison Matin D Series.

540
00:29:29,873 --> 00:29:34,169
Patek Philippe, Louis Vuitton suit.
Cheongdam Louvacity wine bar.

541
00:29:34,295 --> 00:29:37,089
Height between 5'11" and six feet.

542
00:29:37,214 --> 00:29:39,383
It was Wednesday, October 14th.

543
00:29:39,508 --> 00:29:42,720
That's when Song Hae-na said
she couldn't film 'cause she was sick.

544
00:29:43,387 --> 00:29:44,346
Should I go on?

545
00:29:45,347 --> 00:29:46,307
Uh…

546
00:29:51,687 --> 00:29:55,107
[music intensifies]

547
00:29:55,983 --> 00:29:57,818
I told the assistant director about this.

548
00:29:59,028 --> 00:30:00,904
My photo call got moved up.

549
00:30:01,071 --> 00:30:04,617
Out of 22 shoots,
you haven't shown up for seven.

550
00:30:04,742 --> 00:30:05,784
I'm sorry.

551
00:30:06,785 --> 00:30:08,537
You change everything on a whim.

552
00:30:08,662 --> 00:30:11,123
Lines, the shot list,
even the storyboards.

553
00:30:12,082 --> 00:30:14,418
I try to be understanding
since you're a rookie,

554
00:30:14,543 --> 00:30:19,089
but when there are inconsistencies
between the call sheet and the shoot,

555
00:30:19,214 --> 00:30:21,634
-it throws everyone off.
-[breathes deeply]

556
00:30:21,759 --> 00:30:25,721
I figured you needed more time
to avoid all the confusion,

557
00:30:26,180 --> 00:30:28,390
but I held back
and didn't talk to you about it.

558
00:30:28,515 --> 00:30:31,977
I thought it'd put you on the spot.
I was being considerate,

559
00:30:32,102 --> 00:30:34,146
but it caused confusion on your side.

560
00:30:34,271 --> 00:30:35,606
You're saying that it's my fault then?

561
00:30:35,731 --> 00:30:38,025
That's what happens
when you work with an amateur.

562
00:30:38,150 --> 00:30:40,110
Honestly, I should have known better.

563
00:30:40,569 --> 00:30:43,614
The wire set up at the tank
looked quite unsafe earlier.

564
00:30:44,323 --> 00:30:48,077
How can I work in an unsafe set?
Should I risk my life for a single shoot?

565
00:30:48,202 --> 00:30:50,913
The main wire has backup. It's double-set.

566
00:30:51,455 --> 00:30:55,459
We went as far as getting autobraking gear
to maintain tension during depth shifts.

567
00:30:56,710 --> 00:30:59,463
We calculated your weight
to a 0.1 pound margin

568
00:30:59,630 --> 00:31:01,256
and prepared the harness.

569
00:31:03,008 --> 00:31:06,595
Water temp is 75 degrees.
Tank pressure is set.

570
00:31:06,720 --> 00:31:09,765
Two safety divers are also on standby.
All good?

571
00:31:10,849 --> 00:31:16,230
-Block them.
-[all clamoring]

572
00:31:16,939 --> 00:31:17,940
[grunts]

573
00:31:18,399 --> 00:31:21,193
Everyone get ready.
We shoot in five minutes.

574
00:31:24,530 --> 00:31:25,656
[Yeong-rae] I said you can't go in.

575
00:31:25,781 --> 00:31:28,492
-Please calm down while we're shooting.
-[overlapping chatter]

576
00:31:30,035 --> 00:31:32,246
[music crescendos, fades]

577
00:31:32,371 --> 00:31:35,791
Are you out of your mind?
I'm not letting this go.

578
00:31:35,916 --> 00:31:38,752
I know you're doing this on purpose.
[breathes deeply]

579
00:31:39,253 --> 00:31:41,755
Your lover. He's married, right?

580
00:31:42,715 --> 00:31:44,925
Strange how he was more careful
than an actress.

581
00:31:45,384 --> 00:31:47,886
He even switched cars twice on the way.

582
00:31:49,304 --> 00:31:52,057
Your absences always matched
to his schedule.

583
00:31:52,182 --> 00:31:53,350
Always on a Monday.

584
00:31:54,268 --> 00:31:57,354
Every single time you've claimed
to be sick and in terrible shape.

585
00:31:57,479 --> 00:31:59,064
Also, you were hysterical.

586
00:31:59,189 --> 00:32:02,025
-Are you stalking me? Seriously?
-Yeah.

587
00:32:02,735 --> 00:32:04,528
And this is blackmail, okay?

588
00:32:08,031 --> 00:32:09,533
[low somber music playing]

589
00:32:09,658 --> 00:32:13,954
You might see this as just a passing film,
but for me, not the case.

590
00:32:14,913 --> 00:32:16,749
'Cause this is my one shot.

591
00:32:17,291 --> 00:32:19,918
I'm working like my life
depends on this show.

592
00:32:20,502 --> 00:32:21,837
My life at risk here.

593
00:32:26,008 --> 00:32:28,719
If you don't want your life ruined
over dating a married man,

594
00:32:29,344 --> 00:32:31,013
we better start working together.

595
00:32:32,347 --> 00:32:34,016
'Cause I'm not sure what I might do.

596
00:32:37,436 --> 00:32:40,063
-Okay, let's get Hae-na in a harness.
-[crew member] Yes, ma'am.

597
00:32:44,735 --> 00:32:47,154
[harness jangling]

598
00:32:50,657 --> 00:32:52,743
-Get it ready for her safety.
-[crew member] Copy that.

599
00:32:54,244 --> 00:32:55,621
[Hae-na] Director.

600
00:32:57,289 --> 00:33:00,501
[music intensifies]

601
00:33:07,758 --> 00:33:11,094
If you're really that scared
of your life coming to an end,

602
00:33:12,763 --> 00:33:14,556
then I should end it for you.

603
00:33:15,265 --> 00:33:17,518
Goodbye, Madam Director.

604
00:33:23,899 --> 00:33:26,985
-[gasps]
-[crew members screaming, shouting]

605
00:33:28,153 --> 00:33:29,863
[gasps]

606
00:33:31,281 --> 00:33:33,617
[indistinct murmuring]

607
00:33:35,410 --> 00:33:40,207
[breathes shakily]

608
00:33:45,379 --> 00:33:50,050
[breathes deeply]

609
00:33:52,261 --> 00:33:53,345
[sighs]

610
00:33:54,555 --> 00:33:56,890
[music concludes]

611
00:33:57,683 --> 00:34:00,352
[dogs barking in distance]

612
00:34:00,477 --> 00:34:01,687
[cell phone vibrates]

613
00:34:03,814 --> 00:34:05,607
[Namgung]  Yeong-do says
we're out of beer, so hurry.

614
00:34:05,732 --> 00:34:07,776
Where are you? I'll pick you up.

615
00:34:07,901 --> 00:34:11,071
[funky music playing over cell phone]

616
00:34:12,155 --> 00:34:15,742
This is what
it's all about, guys! [screams]

617
00:34:16,618 --> 00:34:17,870
You freaked me out!

618
00:34:18,787 --> 00:34:19,955
[gasps]

619
00:34:20,747 --> 00:34:22,583
-What?
-[sighs]

620
00:34:24,751 --> 00:34:25,878
-[snorts]
-[music concludes]

621
00:34:26,503 --> 00:34:30,340
The street lighting is terrible.
Top-down lighting ruins everything.

622
00:34:32,050 --> 00:34:35,095
I saw some of your videos.
You've got a good eye.

623
00:34:35,470 --> 00:34:37,431
The thing you have is no taste.

624
00:34:37,556 --> 00:34:40,517
Whatever. It's just a hobby.

625
00:34:41,393 --> 00:34:44,229
-I'll probably quit after a few.
-[chuckles softly]

626
00:34:44,354 --> 00:34:48,650
You got your lying abilities from your mom
and your incompetence from your dad.

627
00:34:48,775 --> 00:34:49,693
That's on you.

628
00:34:49,818 --> 00:34:51,820
Everyone's trashing me
saying I take after you.

629
00:34:51,945 --> 00:34:53,280
Oh, yeah, right.

630
00:34:53,906 --> 00:34:58,285
Auntie, were you a bully in kindergarten?

631
00:34:58,410 --> 00:34:59,786
[Yeong-do over video]  Look, don't forget.

632
00:34:59,912 --> 00:35:02,039
Mi-do got freaking kicked out
of kindergarten.

633
00:35:02,164 --> 00:35:03,540
-Twice, actually.
-Oh, jeez.

634
00:35:03,665 --> 00:35:04,499
Yeah?

635
00:35:04,625 --> 00:35:07,377
You do know she walks around
with trash in her pockets, right?

636
00:35:07,544 --> 00:35:09,463
It's actually fun taking it all out.

637
00:35:10,589 --> 00:35:13,216
Oh, and she wore the same socks
for three days.

638
00:35:13,342 --> 00:35:16,553
-I saw it. It's true. You saw it too?
-[Namgung laughs]  She still does that.

639
00:35:16,678 --> 00:35:19,473
But just a few times,
and she never goes past four days.

640
00:35:19,598 --> 00:35:22,059
-And you're okay with that?
-[bright whimsical music playing]

641
00:35:22,184 --> 00:35:24,269
You still want to marry her, Namgung?

642
00:35:24,394 --> 00:35:26,563
[Wan-do] Hey, hey, hey. Give it up.

643
00:35:26,688 --> 00:35:30,400
We've already listed 72 of her flaws,
but he's still sure.

644
00:35:30,525 --> 00:35:31,526
That's true love.

645
00:35:34,279 --> 00:35:35,280
[sighs]

646
00:35:36,531 --> 00:35:39,910
Hey, if you're gonna marry her,
you'd be better off becoming a monk.

647
00:35:40,786 --> 00:35:42,829
[Namgung]  Don't say things
like that in front of her.

648
00:35:42,996 --> 00:35:45,248
She acts tough, but she really gets hurt.

649
00:35:45,374 --> 00:35:47,542
-But she brings it on herself.
-Careful now.

650
00:35:50,796 --> 00:35:55,384
[sighs] Hey, each time you see Mi-do,
does your heart still flutter?

651
00:35:55,509 --> 00:35:57,844
Does it go thump, thump, pitter-patter?

652
00:35:58,011 --> 00:35:58,929
Hmm.

653
00:36:03,517 --> 00:36:04,559
[music concludes]

654
00:36:04,685 --> 00:36:07,229
Mm-hmm. It still flutters.

655
00:36:08,146 --> 00:36:12,025
I miss her when she's not around,
and I feel empty without her.

656
00:36:12,150 --> 00:36:17,155
Even if we're together 24/7,
time flies by. I never get sick of her.

657
00:36:17,823 --> 00:36:21,451
-Shocking, right? I'm shocked as well.
-[tender piano music playing]

658
00:36:22,244 --> 00:36:23,495
[Namgung sighs over video]

659
00:36:25,122 --> 00:36:26,999
HUNMIN CONFECTIONERY

660
00:36:27,165 --> 00:36:28,583
[music concludes]

661
00:36:32,045 --> 00:36:33,130
[sighs]

662
00:36:35,507 --> 00:36:36,508
Sir…

663
00:36:38,051 --> 00:36:41,304
how could you stab me
in the back like this? [scoffs]

664
00:36:42,097 --> 00:36:43,557
Why would you even do that?

665
00:36:43,932 --> 00:36:46,309
We already agreed
to postpone the schedule.

666
00:36:47,561 --> 00:36:51,565
One, you backed off asking
General Manager Kang for a delay.

667
00:36:52,065 --> 00:36:55,986
Two, you backed off from meeting
the year-end release timeline.

668
00:36:57,070 --> 00:37:00,532
Three, next month TF Snack Teams One
and Five are dropping their products.

669
00:37:02,743 --> 00:37:05,037
So please tell me, what's the reason?

670
00:37:05,162 --> 00:37:06,747
-That way I can--
-[Su-a] Or four.

671
00:37:07,831 --> 00:37:11,710
He backed off because the sample
from Snack Team Five was high quality.

672
00:37:16,590 --> 00:37:17,507
Uh…

673
00:37:18,383 --> 00:37:19,342
I'm sorry.

674
00:37:20,093 --> 00:37:21,720
You're not my manager.
[chuckles awkwardly]

675
00:37:26,516 --> 00:37:27,642
I apologize.

676
00:37:37,194 --> 00:37:39,696
Team Five's sample
cannot be that excellent.

677
00:37:41,364 --> 00:37:43,784
The sample that came out yesterday is.

678
00:37:43,909 --> 00:37:45,285
-Yesterday?
-I got to taste it.

679
00:37:45,410 --> 00:37:46,536
We share a research team.

680
00:37:47,287 --> 00:37:49,831
The previous version lacked
a sweet and salty balance,

681
00:37:49,956 --> 00:37:51,166
but they really improved it.

682
00:37:52,209 --> 00:37:56,671
Uh, the aftertaste is good
and has a bold flavor.

683
00:37:58,006 --> 00:38:00,383
I bet their survey results
will beat your team's, too.

684
00:38:02,677 --> 00:38:03,720
Hmm.

685
00:38:04,721 --> 00:38:06,973
You wrote "my condolences," did you?

686
00:38:08,767 --> 00:38:11,061
Snack Team Four, Park Su-a.

687
00:38:11,686 --> 00:38:13,063
TF Snack Team Three,

688
00:38:14,356 --> 00:38:16,066
Assistant Manager Namgung Ho.

689
00:38:19,569 --> 00:38:22,155
The reason the fourth sample had issues…

690
00:38:23,156 --> 00:38:24,449
I know what it is.

691
00:38:25,450 --> 00:38:26,827
Do you wanna know?

692
00:38:34,167 --> 00:38:39,339
[automated voice speaking indistinctly
over screen]

693
00:38:39,464 --> 00:38:40,423
WHEN THAT DAY COMES

694
00:38:40,549 --> 00:38:42,592
[automated voice]  This summer,
one decision will change everything.

695
00:38:42,717 --> 00:38:44,219
This summer, the past comes back.

696
00:38:44,344 --> 00:38:47,806
[cell phone vibrating]

697
00:38:47,931 --> 00:38:50,934
INCOMING CALL

698
00:38:51,101 --> 00:38:53,228
[cell phone continues vibrating]

699
00:38:53,395 --> 00:38:54,521
[soft music playing over speakers]

700
00:38:54,646 --> 00:38:55,981
[Tae-seung] Nice to meet you.

701
00:38:56,106 --> 00:38:59,192
I'm the attorney for Nobu Film.
Han Tae-seung, a pleasure.

702
00:38:59,776 --> 00:39:00,819
[chuckles softly]

703
00:39:04,406 --> 00:39:08,869
This is our draft of the settlement.
I thought it best to offer it first.

704
00:39:09,828 --> 00:39:10,829
SETTLEMENT AGREEMENT

705
00:39:10,954 --> 00:39:15,584
Take a look, and let me know if you have
any kind of questions or revisions.

706
00:39:17,169 --> 00:39:19,588
[pensive instrumental music playing]

707
00:39:19,713 --> 00:39:25,010
The directing fee won't be paid in full,
and a three percent copyright stake?

708
00:39:25,135 --> 00:39:28,013
My client's aware
that you are the one at fault here,

709
00:39:28,138 --> 00:39:29,973
so we ask for your understanding.

710
00:39:30,098 --> 00:39:31,683
This is absurd. I can't.

711
00:39:33,018 --> 00:39:35,312
[inhales deeply]
Because you forced the shoot,

712
00:39:35,437 --> 00:39:37,898
Song Hae-na sustained
an injury during filming.

713
00:39:38,023 --> 00:39:41,359
That situation left her suffering
from mental distress,

714
00:39:41,484 --> 00:39:43,111
and she refused to finish the film.

715
00:39:44,362 --> 00:39:46,865
So naturally, you're the one
who's responsible for all this.

716
00:39:46,990 --> 00:39:47,991
[scoffs]

717
00:39:48,575 --> 00:39:51,494
Anyone who heard you
would think she broke a leg.

718
00:39:51,620 --> 00:39:55,373
That's not all. Don't forget your exit
caused bigger losses than expected,

719
00:39:55,498 --> 00:39:58,877
including wages of more
than 40 crew members for two months.

720
00:39:59,002 --> 00:40:02,422
The soundstage rental alone cost
over 300 million won.

721
00:40:06,718 --> 00:40:09,679
What if I don't agree to this settlement,
and I don't sign?

722
00:40:09,804 --> 00:40:14,059
I can't say for sure,
but maybe around next month,

723
00:40:14,184 --> 00:40:17,312
an article titled,
"Lee Mi-do, director of the film  No Heart,

724
00:40:17,437 --> 00:40:19,898
fired for incompetence,"
will probably be published.

725
00:40:21,149 --> 00:40:22,400
But if you sign, it can change to,

726
00:40:22,525 --> 00:40:25,570
"Director Lee Mi-do leaves  No Heart
due to health reason."

727
00:40:26,404 --> 00:40:27,572
[chuckles]

728
00:40:27,697 --> 00:40:29,699
That's a lot more flattering
than being fired.

729
00:40:30,617 --> 00:40:31,576
Right?

730
00:40:32,327 --> 00:40:34,996
But of course, the choice
is completely your call.

731
00:40:35,121 --> 00:40:37,415
But sadly, we don't have much time left.

732
00:40:37,916 --> 00:40:39,584
So I'll need your answer by next week

733
00:40:39,709 --> 00:40:41,127
-at the latest.
-[knocking on door]

734
00:40:42,254 --> 00:40:43,380
[door opens]

735
00:40:46,716 --> 00:40:47,968
[music fades]

736
00:40:48,093 --> 00:40:51,096
-What? What do you want?
-Sorry.

737
00:40:51,721 --> 00:40:55,016
-I came in because you rang. Did you not?
-What?

738
00:40:55,976 --> 00:40:59,020
I'm the one who rang.
I can order freely, right?

739
00:41:00,146 --> 00:41:01,731
[sighs]

740
00:41:01,856 --> 00:41:04,818
Hmm… [inhales sharply]

741
00:41:04,943 --> 00:41:10,156
One bottle of your finest scotch,
also bring some fruit on the side.

742
00:41:10,282 --> 00:41:12,284
-And ice and sparkling water.
-[waiter] Yes.

743
00:41:12,409 --> 00:41:14,619
-I'll prepare that right away.
-[Mi-do] Mm.

744
00:41:15,704 --> 00:41:18,373
I'll get the final settlement
to you next week.

745
00:41:18,498 --> 00:41:20,292
You seem busy, so you can leave.

746
00:41:21,960 --> 00:41:23,169
[sighs]

747
00:41:23,837 --> 00:41:24,838
[scoffs]

748
00:41:27,549 --> 00:41:29,634
[soft music playing over speakers]

749
00:41:29,759 --> 00:41:33,263
Do you remember Chairman Choi's case
from last year?

750
00:41:33,805 --> 00:41:36,391
Back then, the prosecution
also talked about intent,

751
00:41:36,975 --> 00:41:39,019
but we got a no-charge disposition.

752
00:41:40,186 --> 00:41:41,646
Just leave it all to me

753
00:41:41,771 --> 00:41:43,815
-and go prepare for your next gig.
-[knocking on door]

754
00:41:45,400 --> 00:41:46,359
Yeah?

755
00:41:54,826 --> 00:41:55,744
[chuckles]

756
00:41:56,619 --> 00:41:58,913
Shit. How many bottles
are we talking about here?

757
00:41:59,039 --> 00:42:02,208
Two Monterio 21s, one 30-year,
and the first bottle of Ravelo.

758
00:42:02,334 --> 00:42:06,546
-[upbeat pop music playing over speakers]
-[all shouting, cheering]

759
00:42:21,394 --> 00:42:22,771
[shouting, cheering fades]

760
00:42:22,896 --> 00:42:24,981
[dramatic music playing over speakers]

761
00:42:25,106 --> 00:42:26,358
What would you like to do?

762
00:42:28,068 --> 00:42:30,570
[sighs] Don't let them order anymore.

763
00:42:31,196 --> 00:42:32,405
[waiter] Of course, sir.

764
00:42:38,953 --> 00:42:40,914
She's a fucking lunatic.

765
00:42:42,123 --> 00:42:44,542
[all sigh]

766
00:42:44,667 --> 00:42:47,379
-[indistinct chatter over TV]
-[sighs]

767
00:42:49,005 --> 00:42:51,257
Are you going
to sign the settlement, director?

768
00:42:51,383 --> 00:42:53,468
Are you crazy? Why would she do that?

769
00:42:53,593 --> 00:42:55,637
[Guk-jin] Still, this tyranny
from the production company

770
00:42:55,762 --> 00:42:56,721
and the actor.

771
00:42:56,846 --> 00:42:59,265
We need to just expose everything
to the world.

772
00:42:59,391 --> 00:43:01,935
Hey, that's a terrible idea.
If this blows up,

773
00:43:02,060 --> 00:43:03,269
it'll only make things harder for her.

774
00:43:03,395 --> 00:43:04,521
[Jang-mi] Shut up for one second.

775
00:43:04,646 --> 00:43:06,523
-You're way too loud.
-Guys, just stop.

776
00:43:06,648 --> 00:43:11,319
All of you, stop reporting to my set.
That's why I called you.

777
00:43:12,862 --> 00:43:15,573
I only hired you for a bit
because I was short on staff.

778
00:43:15,698 --> 00:43:16,908
I wasn't keeping you.

779
00:43:17,909 --> 00:43:19,828
My director friend
is filming something new,

780
00:43:19,953 --> 00:43:21,746
and I asked him to hire the three of you.

781
00:43:22,455 --> 00:43:25,417
Go do your damn best, okay?
Don't put me on the spot.

782
00:43:25,834 --> 00:43:30,588
No, I don't want to.
I want to keep working with you, director.

783
00:43:30,713 --> 00:43:32,841
Lee Guk-jin, stop the complaining.

784
00:43:32,966 --> 00:43:35,385
If you have time for that,
go write a screenplay.

785
00:43:36,010 --> 00:43:37,846
-Mm.
-Go, go, go. Let's go.

786
00:43:42,267 --> 00:43:43,726
[whimsical instrumental music playing]

787
00:43:43,852 --> 00:43:46,646
Huh? Hey, bae.

788
00:43:51,484 --> 00:43:52,944
[breathes heavily]

789
00:44:00,535 --> 00:44:03,663
[police officer] Now tell me,
how did you know they were there?

790
00:44:03,788 --> 00:44:05,915
-[music concludes]
-They practically flaunted it online.

791
00:44:06,040 --> 00:44:08,042
[police officer] So you saw the post
on her socials and went?

792
00:44:08,168 --> 00:44:10,211
-Who threw the first punch?
-This jerk did.

793
00:44:10,336 --> 00:44:12,797
-He came at me, no warning.
-She was cheating on me.

794
00:44:12,964 --> 00:44:14,048
How could I not be mad about it?

795
00:44:14,174 --> 00:44:16,593
I've already told you a thousand times,
that's not it,

796
00:44:16,718 --> 00:44:17,927
-all right?
-Hey!

797
00:44:19,095 --> 00:44:21,848
-Then what were you doing, huh?
-That's enough already.

798
00:44:23,141 --> 00:44:24,934
It's all because of you.

799
00:44:25,059 --> 00:44:27,562
Fired from your own movie
and shooting porn.

800
00:44:27,687 --> 00:44:28,897
You should be ashamed.

801
00:44:29,063 --> 00:44:31,232
Why use her as your staff
in a place like that?

802
00:44:32,025 --> 00:44:34,068
Ruin your own life if you want to.

803
00:44:34,194 --> 00:44:36,613
Shooting an adult film isn't embarrassing.

804
00:44:36,738 --> 00:44:38,573
Your behavior right now is.

805
00:44:38,698 --> 00:44:41,409
-[scoffs]
-And Jang-mi doesn't deserve this.

806
00:44:41,534 --> 00:44:44,204
What? Don't speak to me like…

807
00:44:45,205 --> 00:44:46,456
What are you doing?

808
00:44:49,167 --> 00:44:51,211
[groans loudly]

809
00:44:53,630 --> 00:44:55,590
-[sighs]
-[Jang-mi's boyfriend whimpers]

810
00:44:59,052 --> 00:45:00,053
[sighs]

811
00:45:05,391 --> 00:45:06,893
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

812
00:45:07,769 --> 00:45:10,480
But I can explain. [breathes heavily]

813
00:45:11,397 --> 00:45:13,441
I heard it all. No need to explain.

814
00:45:14,317 --> 00:45:16,778
Looks like you
and Song Hae-na clashed again.

815
00:45:16,903 --> 00:45:18,696
And you need money for a lawyer.

816
00:45:18,821 --> 00:45:21,574
So you decided to go behind my back
and did an adult film.

817
00:45:22,575 --> 00:45:25,537
-I'm sorry.
-Is Yeon-ju the PD?

818
00:45:28,665 --> 00:45:31,125
Are you crazy? What are you doing?

819
00:45:31,251 --> 00:45:34,295
They haven't found a director yet.
This is your last chance.

820
00:45:39,968 --> 00:45:41,135
[sighs]

821
00:45:41,928 --> 00:45:42,971
[sighs]

822
00:45:44,180 --> 00:45:46,724
How will you face your mom
after this mess, huh?

823
00:45:48,059 --> 00:45:50,103
How are you gonna
explain this to everyone?

824
00:45:50,728 --> 00:45:53,481
How will you lie to yourself
and pretend you're okay?

825
00:45:54,232 --> 00:45:57,026
You're not okay.
You need to understand that.

826
00:45:57,151 --> 00:45:59,946
So it isn't okay if I fail?
It does matter.

827
00:46:00,071 --> 00:46:02,824
Not to me. It does to you.

828
00:46:02,949 --> 00:46:04,200
Don't you care about that?

829
00:46:05,368 --> 00:46:08,830
Why would you let some random idiot
tell you you're ruining your life?

830
00:46:10,582 --> 00:46:12,333
I made myself clear.

831
00:46:13,334 --> 00:46:14,460
What did I tell you?

832
00:46:15,211 --> 00:46:18,715
Do your best with no regrets.

833
00:46:18,840 --> 00:46:21,050
But you will regret this. I know you will.

834
00:46:22,802 --> 00:46:23,928
I'll handle it.

835
00:46:25,179 --> 00:46:27,807
This is my job.
It's none of your business.

836
00:46:27,932 --> 00:46:30,393
Then just stop doing things that worry me!

837
00:46:32,353 --> 00:46:35,523
-[somber piano music playing]
-[scoffs]

838
00:46:38,067 --> 00:46:39,944
Look where handling it got you.

839
00:46:40,486 --> 00:46:41,821
This is the result.

840
00:46:42,572 --> 00:46:44,073
How can I do nothing?

841
00:46:44,198 --> 00:46:46,659
You should have told me first.
I could have helped you to--

842
00:46:46,784 --> 00:46:48,536
I didn't want you to see it.

843
00:46:50,455 --> 00:46:53,207
This side of me is too pathetic
for you to see.

844
00:46:53,333 --> 00:46:55,877
[breathes heavily]

845
00:46:56,002 --> 00:46:57,503
And I'm too ashamed of it.

846
00:47:01,466 --> 00:47:02,467
[sighs]

847
00:47:04,302 --> 00:47:06,054
So this is how it feels.

848
00:47:06,179 --> 00:47:09,432
[breathes heavily]

849
00:47:09,557 --> 00:47:10,642
[sighs]

850
00:47:10,767 --> 00:47:12,935
[breathes deeply]

851
00:47:25,323 --> 00:47:27,617
[door lock beeping]

852
00:47:28,826 --> 00:47:32,080
[breathes deeply]

853
00:47:33,831 --> 00:47:35,124
Mi-do, listen.

854
00:47:35,249 --> 00:47:37,585
[music concludes]

855
00:47:39,295 --> 00:47:42,590
-I understand, let's--
-Let's end it, now.

856
00:47:46,511 --> 00:47:49,722
-Wait, Mi-do…
-I need to end our relationship.

857
00:47:50,932 --> 00:47:51,974
[sighs]

858
00:47:54,769 --> 00:47:56,396
Look, I was wrong earlier.

859
00:47:58,106 --> 00:48:00,149
I shouldn't have talked to you like that.

860
00:48:01,609 --> 00:48:04,654
I was only thinking of myself. I get it.

861
00:48:05,196 --> 00:48:06,447
When did it start?

862
00:48:08,533 --> 00:48:12,704
You said I was your driving force
and compass. Tell me since when.

863
00:48:14,288 --> 00:48:15,623
[poignant instrumental music playing]

864
00:48:15,748 --> 00:48:17,959
[Namgung over video]
Hmm. I still get butterflies.

865
00:48:18,084 --> 00:48:19,836
How is this possible?

866
00:48:19,961 --> 00:48:21,045
It amazes me too.

867
00:48:23,548 --> 00:48:25,758
I'd love to say that, but it's not true.

868
00:48:25,883 --> 00:48:27,677
[Yeong-do]  Man, I thought it was true.

869
00:48:27,802 --> 00:48:29,804
[Wan-do]  So you don't get
butterflies anymore?

870
00:48:29,929 --> 00:48:31,723
[Namgung]  I've been with Mi-do
for ten years,

871
00:48:31,848 --> 00:48:33,474
so it'd be weird if I still did.

872
00:48:36,102 --> 00:48:40,398
To me, Mi-do is my reason
for staying loyal to a company.

873
00:48:40,982 --> 00:48:42,358
She's my life's compass.

874
00:48:44,152 --> 00:48:48,698
Whenever I think about quitting my job,
she's the force that keeps me going.

875
00:48:51,075 --> 00:48:56,330
So I see her as the compass that keeps me
from straying off the right path.

876
00:48:59,333 --> 00:49:01,878
I just have to get through
another 30 years.

877
00:49:03,004 --> 00:49:06,132
[chuckles]  I want to grow old fast.

878
00:49:12,180 --> 00:49:13,264
[sighs]

879
00:49:14,974 --> 00:49:18,728
I'm a heavy burden to you.
It's too much to handle.

880
00:49:19,687 --> 00:49:21,355
This is for the best.

881
00:49:21,481 --> 00:49:23,149
[sighs] Listen, Mi-do.

882
00:49:24,484 --> 00:49:27,528
It's not like that.
That's not really what I meant.

883
00:49:29,071 --> 00:49:31,365
You know exactly how I feel, don't you?

884
00:49:33,493 --> 00:49:35,286
I know the butterflies are gone.

885
00:49:36,287 --> 00:49:37,872
You said so yourself.

886
00:49:38,956 --> 00:49:41,334
Seeing me doesn't get
to you anymore, does it?

887
00:49:41,459 --> 00:49:44,170
Does your heart race? It doesn't.

888
00:49:44,921 --> 00:49:46,923
We've been together for ten years now.

889
00:49:47,423 --> 00:49:48,925
That's normal, you know?

890
00:49:49,884 --> 00:49:54,305
Namgung, do you know why
I wasn't a burden that day?

891
00:49:54,430 --> 00:49:56,682
You loved me, so I wasn't happy.

892
00:50:03,064 --> 00:50:04,982
So you've made up your mind, right?

893
00:50:06,984 --> 00:50:09,028
So this is it, you're really ending us?

894
00:50:13,866 --> 00:50:14,951
It's true.

895
00:50:16,786 --> 00:50:18,287
We've changed, I know that.

896
00:50:18,412 --> 00:50:23,000
Yet… everything we've been through
doesn't just go away.

897
00:50:23,125 --> 00:50:27,588
It's not like we don't love each other.
I mean, everyone goes through that.

898
00:50:27,713 --> 00:50:29,590
How can we stay passionate forever?

899
00:50:35,012 --> 00:50:36,264
I will try harder.

900
00:50:41,018 --> 00:50:42,061
Mi-do…

901
00:50:44,355 --> 00:50:47,817
I think I've been neglecting you.

902
00:50:48,025 --> 00:50:50,319
[poignant instrumental music continues]

903
00:50:50,444 --> 00:50:52,989
So I'll try three times as hard, I swear.

904
00:50:53,114 --> 00:50:54,907
Then I'll be three times heavier.

905
00:50:57,285 --> 00:50:59,412
And I'll feel worse than I already do.

906
00:51:06,460 --> 00:51:07,545
Namgung…

907
00:51:09,589 --> 00:51:11,173
can't you see that…

908
00:51:12,633 --> 00:51:16,554
your sense of responsibility,
obligation, and remorse…

909
00:51:17,638 --> 00:51:19,348
highlight how pathetic I am?

910
00:51:21,976 --> 00:51:23,978
And now I think I hate myself.

911
00:51:25,980 --> 00:51:26,939
What?

912
00:51:27,398 --> 00:51:31,152
You know… I have to be
so careful around you.

913
00:51:32,987 --> 00:51:37,491
It's easy to confuse being careful
around someone with being considerate.

914
00:51:38,534 --> 00:51:41,454
Being considered
makes me feel like I'm good.

915
00:51:43,706 --> 00:51:46,584
But when I'm too careful around someone,
I feel pathetic.

916
00:51:50,212 --> 00:51:53,049
And if I feel any more pathetic,
I'm afraid I'll lose it.

917
00:51:54,675 --> 00:51:55,676
Mm.

918
00:51:59,889 --> 00:52:02,141
That's why we should end all this.

919
00:52:05,227 --> 00:52:07,229
So my love makes you feel pathetic?

920
00:52:11,651 --> 00:52:12,693
[scoffs]

921
00:52:17,573 --> 00:52:19,492
So you really want to break up with me?

922
00:52:22,161 --> 00:52:23,496
[music concludes]

923
00:52:23,621 --> 00:52:24,664
Mm.

924
00:52:25,164 --> 00:52:26,999
You're completely sure then, is that it?

925
00:52:30,711 --> 00:52:31,837
[sighs]

926
00:52:35,383 --> 00:52:36,842
Last time I'll ask.

927
00:52:38,970 --> 00:52:40,096
Think carefully.

928
00:52:43,641 --> 00:52:45,226
Do you really want to end it?

929
00:52:47,937 --> 00:52:50,022
Mm. I do.

930
00:52:56,779 --> 00:52:57,738
Okay.

931
00:53:00,533 --> 00:53:02,076
Fine. Good luck.

932
00:53:10,543 --> 00:53:12,920
[door lock beeping]

933
00:53:13,087 --> 00:53:16,716
[sobbing]

934
00:53:21,262 --> 00:53:25,224
[sobbing]

935
00:53:25,349 --> 00:53:29,687
-[somber instrumental music playing]
-[vocalist singing in Korean]

936
00:53:33,774 --> 00:53:35,443
[breathes deeply]

937
00:53:36,861 --> 00:53:42,533
[sobbing]

938
00:53:48,456 --> 00:53:51,042
[breathes deeply]

939
00:53:53,002 --> 00:53:54,086
[sighs]

940
00:53:54,503 --> 00:53:56,714
LOVING YOU
WAS THE BEST THING I'VE EVER DONE

941
00:53:56,839 --> 00:53:59,550
IT'S BEEN TEN YEARS,
BUT I'M STILL GETTING TO KNOW YOU

942
00:53:59,675 --> 00:54:02,720
LET'S KEEP BEING US AND STAY TOGETHER
I LOVE YOU

943
00:54:05,931 --> 00:54:09,018
[Mi-do]  Our time together
was as bright as the sun.

944
00:54:09,602 --> 00:54:12,063
Our time together was so beautiful…

945
00:54:13,647 --> 00:54:15,024
that nothing's changed.

946
00:54:15,983 --> 00:54:17,276
It's still the same.

947
00:54:18,444 --> 00:54:21,405
I fooled myself, and I fooled you.

948
00:54:21,530 --> 00:54:25,451
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

949
00:54:31,165 --> 00:54:32,083
[Mi-do grunts softly]

950
00:54:34,418 --> 00:54:39,090
[sighs, grunts]

951
00:54:39,215 --> 00:54:40,716
But we both know something.

952
00:54:42,009 --> 00:54:44,970
The love between us doesn't shine anymore.

953
00:54:48,974 --> 00:54:51,393
The weight of our love is suffocating.

954
00:54:52,269 --> 00:54:53,729
It's withered and pathetic.

955
00:54:53,896 --> 00:54:56,857
[cell phone vibrating]

956
00:54:56,982 --> 00:54:59,110
MY BABY

957
00:55:00,694 --> 00:55:01,779
[Wan-do sighs]

958
00:55:02,738 --> 00:55:04,406
-They picking up?
-Hmm.

959
00:55:06,117 --> 00:55:07,952
-Are you for real?
-Mm.

960
00:55:08,619 --> 00:55:11,539
-Did those two get into a fight?
-Ah, shit.

961
00:55:12,206 --> 00:55:13,207
What do we do?

962
00:55:13,332 --> 00:55:16,502
What do you mean? Everything's ready.

963
00:55:18,379 --> 00:55:19,713
Try calling again.

964
00:55:19,839 --> 00:55:22,800
TO THE ONE ALWAYS BY MY SIDE

965
00:55:23,968 --> 00:55:25,136
[Wan-do] Ah, damn.

966
00:55:25,261 --> 00:55:27,346
MI-DO, WILL YOU MARRY ME?

967
00:55:27,513 --> 00:55:31,183
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

968
00:55:46,073 --> 00:55:48,367
[Mi-do sobbing]

969
00:56:08,053 --> 00:56:09,513
[exhales heavily]

970
00:56:21,442 --> 00:56:25,738
Just like that,
our ten-year relationship ended.

971
00:56:34,663 --> 00:56:38,876
[groans softly]

972
00:56:40,127 --> 00:56:45,382
[cell phone vibrating]

973
00:56:45,507 --> 00:56:47,051
NAMGUNG-TUSH

974
00:56:47,301 --> 00:56:48,552
[music concludes]

975
00:56:48,677 --> 00:56:50,221
[Mi-do] Good morning.

976
00:56:50,346 --> 00:56:52,932
Wakey, wakey.

977
00:56:53,057 --> 00:56:55,100
[groans] I'm getting up.

978
00:56:56,435 --> 00:56:59,188
I love you, sweetie. Ciao, ciao.

979
00:56:59,313 --> 00:57:02,775
Hmm. I love you, sweetie. Ciao, ciao.

980
00:57:09,573 --> 00:57:12,910
-[gasps]
-[upbeat rock music playing]

981
00:57:16,247 --> 00:57:18,040
[Mi-do screams]

982
00:57:18,165 --> 00:57:19,917
[screams]

983
00:57:20,918 --> 00:57:24,380
[breathes heavily]

984
00:57:24,505 --> 00:57:25,464
Oh!

985
00:57:28,509 --> 00:57:32,554
[breathes heavily]

986
00:57:32,721 --> 00:57:33,722
[Namgung groans]

987
00:57:37,810 --> 00:57:38,978
[music concludes]

988
00:57:43,983 --> 00:57:45,359
[woman 1] Oh, it's snowing.

989
00:57:45,484 --> 00:57:46,318
SHORT FILM SCREENING

990
00:57:46,443 --> 00:57:49,196
[man] Whoa. So today
is the first snow in Seoul.

991
00:57:49,321 --> 00:57:50,614
The weathermen called it.

992
00:57:51,448 --> 00:57:52,616
DIRECTOR LEE MI-DO

993
00:57:54,118 --> 00:57:55,619
LOOKING FORWARD TO YOUR NEXT FILM

994
00:57:55,744 --> 00:57:57,037
WISHING YOU GOOD HEALTH

995
00:57:57,871 --> 00:58:00,624
Excuse me. Did you see who wrote this?

996
00:58:01,750 --> 00:58:05,337
Uh… [inhales sharply]
He just left a little while ago.

997
00:58:05,462 --> 00:58:07,006
[Mi-do gasps]

998
00:58:07,131 --> 00:58:09,591
[woman 2] Wait, Ms. Lee,
your interview starts soon.

999
00:58:09,717 --> 00:58:10,801
Director Lee!

1000
00:58:10,926 --> 00:58:13,178
[panting]

1001
00:58:13,929 --> 00:58:16,307
AFTER SPRING COMES WINTER

1002
00:58:16,473 --> 00:58:20,936
[panting]

1003
00:58:21,061 --> 00:58:21,979
[gasps]

1004
00:58:24,148 --> 00:58:26,108
[Yeong-do sighs]  He's going to Australia.

1005
00:58:26,650 --> 00:58:29,820
One of his classmates
is running a big Korean restaurant there.

1006
00:58:30,487 --> 00:58:32,448
He reached out
to go into business together.

1007
00:58:35,409 --> 00:58:37,536
He says he can never be friends with you.

1008
00:58:38,954 --> 00:58:42,541
He says he's tired of it.
He hates Korea because of you.

1009
00:58:42,666 --> 00:58:45,210
[breathes deeply]

1010
00:58:45,419 --> 00:58:47,212
[Yeong-do]
He'll come back once he's over you.

1011
00:58:49,590 --> 00:58:51,133
[sobs]

1012
00:58:51,258 --> 00:58:54,595
[tender piano music playing]

1013
00:58:54,720 --> 00:58:57,639
[sniffles, breathes deeply]

1014
00:59:00,768 --> 00:59:03,812
[announcer over PA]
The next buses arriving are in 12 minutes

1015
00:59:03,979 --> 00:59:05,773
and 45 minutes.

1016
00:59:09,610 --> 00:59:11,779
[breathes deeply]

1017
00:59:11,904 --> 00:59:12,988
[gasps]

1018
00:59:13,364 --> 00:59:15,741
[breathes heavily]

1019
00:59:19,119 --> 00:59:20,454
You were following me.

1020
00:59:21,288 --> 00:59:23,082
You should have followed me all the way.

1021
00:59:23,957 --> 00:59:25,042
[sighs]

1022
00:59:25,959 --> 00:59:27,586
Mi-do, you're something else.

1023
00:59:28,504 --> 00:59:32,925
If I don't come to you,
then you won't come to me.

1024
00:59:34,343 --> 00:59:36,595
You said you wouldn't be friends with me.

1025
00:59:36,720 --> 00:59:37,805
Yeah, I won't.

1026
00:59:39,014 --> 00:59:40,182
I won't.

1027
00:59:41,934 --> 00:59:43,894
You really are such a pain in the ass.

1028
00:59:45,229 --> 00:59:46,647
[sniffles]

1029
00:59:49,316 --> 00:59:51,485
But I'm pretty sure of what scares you.

1030
00:59:54,405 --> 00:59:55,989
Because I was terrified too.

1031
00:59:57,783 --> 01:00:01,245
Still… listen, Mi-do.

1032
01:00:03,372 --> 01:00:05,374
What you're scared of won't happen.

1033
01:00:08,210 --> 01:00:10,546
The whole dating and breaking up cliché…

1034
01:00:12,673 --> 01:00:14,383
it won't happen to us.

1035
01:00:16,301 --> 01:00:17,719
How can you be so sure?

1036
01:00:20,139 --> 01:00:22,141
'Cause I love you more than anything.

1037
01:00:27,146 --> 01:00:28,939
More than you can even imagine.

1038
01:00:30,983 --> 01:00:33,360
So much that it burns me inside.

1039
01:00:36,655 --> 01:00:38,490
I love you so much that it hurts.

1040
01:00:40,909 --> 01:00:43,537
[breathes deeply]

1041
01:00:46,999 --> 01:00:49,418
[music swells]

1042
01:00:55,007 --> 01:00:58,010
[music softens]

1043
01:01:07,895 --> 01:01:09,480
[music concludes]

1044
01:01:09,605 --> 01:01:12,566
[Mi-do]  That day,
we became more than friends,

1045
01:01:12,691 --> 01:01:15,277
-and the first snow fell in Seoul.
-[dramatic rock music playing]

1046
01:01:15,402 --> 01:01:18,280
[Mi-do]  After that,
our anniversary wasn't a date,

1047
01:01:18,739 --> 01:01:21,241
but the day
the first snow falls in Seoul.

1048
01:01:22,326 --> 01:01:27,581
We welcomed nine first snows together
and loved each other madly.

1049
01:01:29,166 --> 01:01:33,587
But before the tenth first snow,
we broke up.

1050
01:01:35,464 --> 01:01:40,302
[vocalist singing in Korean]

1051
01:01:46,099 --> 01:01:51,230
♪ I hear your voice in the quiet night ♪

1052
01:01:51,730 --> 01:01:52,981
[vocalist continues singing in Korean]

1053
01:01:53,106 --> 01:01:55,359
THANK YOU TO OH DONG-MIN
FOR HIS SPECIAL APPEARANCE

1054
01:01:57,945 --> 01:02:00,072
[Yeong-do sighs]
You're gonna apologize anyway.

1055
01:02:00,197 --> 01:02:02,199
Aren't you worried about Mi-do?

1056
01:02:02,324 --> 01:02:04,076
[Namgung]  Mi-do and I broke up.
You know that.

1057
01:02:04,201 --> 01:02:05,160
[Mi-do]  It could go either way.

1058
01:02:05,285 --> 01:02:06,995
-[Namgung]  Don't make excuses later.
-[Mi-do]  You too.

1059
01:02:07,120 --> 01:02:09,581
The Spicy SweeTato Chips
were really bad.

1060
01:02:09,706 --> 01:02:11,833
I smoke too.
I've smoked since high school.

1061
01:02:11,959 --> 01:02:13,335
Can I bum one?

1062
01:02:13,460 --> 01:02:15,254
[Mi-do]  I'll kill you
if you come here again.

1063
01:02:15,379 --> 01:02:17,714
[Tae-seung]  Since you want it so badly,
I'll see you in court.

1064
01:02:17,839 --> 01:02:18,966
[Namgung]  What is it this time?

1065
01:02:19,091 --> 01:02:21,552
-That's none of your business now.
-I don't want to care anymore.

1066
01:02:22,135 --> 01:02:25,806
[Mi-do]  Where did all that passion go?
Hmm? And the butterflies?

1067
01:02:26,515 --> 01:02:28,517
Where did they fly away to?

1068
01:02:29,142 --> 01:02:31,395
♪ But you fade away ♪

1069
01:02:31,562 --> 01:02:32,729
[music concludes]

